# 14. TECHNICAL IMPLEMENTATION

Build a real, functional application.

Do not create just a static visual prototype.

### Recommended technology

Use:

- React.
- TypeScript.
- Tailwind CSS.
- Modern reusable UI components.
- Supabase for authentication and database.
- A secure AI integration for intelligent recommendations.
- A suitable image storage solution.

### Database architecture

Create proper database tables for:

1. Users.
2. Cooking library.
3. Categories.
4. Recipes.
5. Meal history.
6. Planned meals.
7. Favorites.
8. User preferences.
9. Occasion menus.
10. Nutrition information.

Use proper relationships between records.

Every user's private data must remain private.

Implement row-level security.

A user must never be able to access another user's personal cooking library or meal history.

### AI integration

Use an actual AI integration for personalized recommendations and new recipe discovery.

Keep API keys secure on the server.

Never expose secret API keys in frontend code.

Do not pretend an AI feature works if it is not connected.

If an AI service is unavailable, provide a sensible local fallback for library-only selection.

The fallback must still obey all library restrictions.

### Recommendation engine

The recommendation engine should use structured user data.

Do not send only a vague prompt to an AI model and trust it to remember everything.

Retrieve the actual library and history from the database, then provide the relevant information to the AI.

Validate every recommended dish against the user's actual library before displaying it.

If a returned dish does not match an existing library record, reject it.

For normal selection modes, the application itself must enforce the library-only restriction, not merely rely on the AI behaving correctly.

### Performance

The application should load quickly.

Avoid unnecessarily large libraries and excessive animations.

Optimize food images.

Use lazy loading.

Keep the mobile experience smooth.

